# Story 5: Your First Session (50s)
# Hook: Name a session, work in it, detach -- and it keeps running without you.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-005-your-first-session.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Name a session, work in it, then detach -- and it keeps running without you.

[00:05.0 --> 00:13.0]
Pass a name to rysh and you get a named session. Here we open one called my-project.

[00:13.0 --> 00:21.0]
Work as usual -- run commands, build, test. This pane is a normal shell.

[00:21.0 --> 00:30.0]
Press Ctrl+O for prefix mode, then d to detach. You drop back to your shell, but the session lives on.

[00:30.0 --> 00:39.0]
rysh list-sessions shows it -- still alive, marked detached, with its process ID.

[00:39.0 --> 00:50.0]
Reattach any time with rysh attach my-project. Your output, history, and pane layout are all restored.

